    "lines": [
      {
        "scene": "hook",
        "text": "Sara Blakely started Spanx with $5,000 she had saved selling fax machines.",
        "start": 0.3,
        "seconds": 3.58,
        "window": 4.27,
        "fill": 0.838
      },
      {
        "scene": "idea",
        "text": "Her whole idea was one pair of pantyhose, with the feet cut off.",
        "start": 4.57,
        "seconds": 2.56,
        "window": 3.23,
        "fill": 0.793
      },
      {
        "scene": "patent",
        "text": "She called it Spanx in 2000, in Atlanta, and wrote the patent application herself.",
        "start": 7.8,
        "seconds": 3.59,
        "window": 4.23,
        "fill": 0.849
      },
      {
        "scene": "neiman",
        "text": "Her first big order came from Neiman Marcus. But how far could one product go?",
        "start": 12.03,
        "seconds": 3.56,
        "window": 4.2,
        "fill": 0.848
      },
      {
        "scene": "owned",
        "text": "For years she owned all of it, with no investors. So what was it really worth?",
        "start": 16.23,
        "seconds": 3.24,
        "window": 3.87,
        "fill": 0.837
      },
      {
        "scene": "blackstone",
        "text": "Then in October, the investment firm Blackstone bought most of it.",
        "start": 20.1,
        "seconds": 2.31,
        "window": 2.93,
        "fill": 0.788
      },
      {
        "scene": "payoff",
        "text": "That deal valued Spanx, the company that started with one pair of pantyhose, at $1.2B.",
        "start": 23.03,
        "seconds": 4.52,
        "window": 5.2,
        "fill": 0.869
      },
      {
        "scene": "ending",
        "text": "She kept a big piece too. Scissors or the sales job: which one built Spanx? Remember,",
        "start": 28.23,
        "seconds": 3.69,
        "window": 4.37,
        "fill": 0.844
      }
    ]
  },
